# Requests to the flash-be API. The routes and their replies are in docs/reference/http-endpoints.md.
@backend = http://localhost:8080
# Login is by cookie: a login or sign-up reply sets access_token and refresh_token, and kulala.nvim and the REST Client
# extension keep them for the next request. The API starts with COOKIE_SECURE=false for local development, so the cookies
# work over plain HTTP. In another client, send them back in a Cookie header.

### Backend: liveness (no dependencies, run with `npx nx dev flash-be`)
GET {{backend}}/health

### Backend: readiness (checks Postgres and Redis, needs `npx nx db:up flash-be`)
GET {{backend}}/ready

### Backend: the current sale (the running sale, else the next one to open, else 404; up to SALE_CACHE_MS old; seed one with `npx nx db:seed-sale flash-be --stock=100`)
GET {{backend}}/sales/current

### Backend: one sale by id (replace the id with the one the seed command printed)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### Backend: sign up as a shopper (sets the two cookies; 409 username_taken; the password needs 8 to 128 characters)
POST {{backend}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ana", "password": "a long password" }

### Backend: log in (sets the two cookies; the same reply for a wrong name and a wrong password)
POST {{backend}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ana", "password": "a long password" }

### Backend: who am I? (needs the access_token cookie; 401 not_authenticated once it has ended)
GET {{backend}}/auth/me

### Backend: renew the login (sent only to /auth, with the refresh_token cookie; sets a new pair, and the old refresh token stops working)
POST {{backend}}/auth/refresh

### Backend: log out (ends the session and clears the cookies)
POST {{backend}}/auth/logout

### Backend: log in as an operator (make the account first with `npx nx db:create-operator flash-be --username=ops --password="a long password"`)
POST {{backend}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ops", "password": "correct-horse-battery" }

### Backend: create a sale (needs a login as an operator: 401 not_authenticated without one, 403 forbidden for a shopper, 409 when the window overlaps)
# Optional fields: name, productId, holdSeconds, admitPerSecond.
POST {{backend}}/admin/sales
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stock": 100, "startsAt": "2030-01-01T12:00:00Z", "endsAt": "2030-01-01T13:00:00Z" }

### Backend: list every sale (operator; the one that opens last first, with sold, holdSeconds and admitPerSecond)
GET {{backend}}/admin/sales

### Backend: change a sale (operator; send only the fields to change: name, stock, startsAt, endsAt, holdSeconds, admitPerSecond; 409 sale_locked once it has started and the change moves the start or lowers the stock)
PATCH {{backend}}/admin/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stock": 150 }

### Backend: remove a sale (operator; 409 sale_has_purchases when someone bought; replace the id)
DELETE {{backend}}/admin/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### Backend: join the queue (log in first; replace the sale id; the reply holds your ticket; write requests can answer 429 with Retry-After)
POST {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/queue

### Backend: check your place (send the ticket from the join reply)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/queue/me
x-queue-ticket: paste-the-ticket-here

### Backend: reserve one item (needs the ticket and an admitted user; the reply holds the reservation id and its end)
POST {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/reservations
x-queue-ticket: paste-the-ticket-here

### Backend: pay for the held item (send the reservation id from the reserve reply; sending it again is safe)
POST {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/purchases
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reservationId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001" }

### Backend: did I get it? (purchased, holding or none)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/purchases/me

### Backend: live sale status (Server-Sent Events; stays open, sends an event when the sale changes)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/events

### Backend: live place in the queue (send the ticket from the join reply; stays open)
GET {{backend}}/sales/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/queue/me/events
x-queue-ticket: paste-the-ticket-here
